114	\begin{definition}[Ideal strategy for Magic Square LCS game $\pmod 2$] 
115		See Figure \ref{eq:mermin-peres-magic-square}. Let $A_e$ be the operator which appears on the right-hand side in the same spot as variable $e$ appears on the left-hand side. Set $A_e^{(v)}:= A_e$ for all $v$. Then set $B_e = \bar{A_e}$ (where any choice of basis works for the conjugation).  Set $\ket\psi = \ket{\text{EPR}}^{\otimes 2}$. We define $\{A_e^{(v)}\}, \{B_e \}, \ket\psi$ to be the \emph{ideal strategy} for the Magic Square game $\pmod 2$.
116	\end{definition}
117	Notice that the $B_e$ are defined only up to local isometry, because of the freedom in the choice of basis for conjugation.
