131	The robust self-testing theorem for the Magic Square game is the following.
132	\begin{thm}\label{thm:robust-self-testing-square}
133	The Magic Square game mod $2$ self-tests the ideal strategy with perfect completeness and $O(\e)$-robustness.
134	\end{thm}
135	To prove this, we'll make a direct application of Theorem \ref{thm:robust-self-testing}. However, we'll use the tighter bounds stated in the appendix as Theorem \ref{thm:robust-self-testing-appendix}. We will check that all of its conditions are satisfied by a series of lemmas. 
136	Throughout, let $\G_2$ be the solution group for the Magic Square game over $\Z_2$. We'll start by identifying $\G_2$ as a group of Pauli operators.
